# Thoughts 

- Progress over perfection — a little better than last week is enough
- Stuck on a bug? Walk away for 10 minutes, come back with fresh eyes
- Read the error message slowly before assuming the worst
- Small, dumb projects teach more than you'd think
- You don't have to understand everything today
- Drink water. Seriously. Half of debugging is just being tired
- One line at a time still counts as moving forward
- Compare yourself to who you were last month, not to strangers online
- It's okay to Google the same thing twice (or five times)
- Ship something small — momentum matters more than size
